/*
:name: arr_comb_tmp
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: arr_comb_tmp
:pyrope_top: arr_comb_tmp
*/
// TRACKER — a blocking temp feeding a comb-array store is DROPPED by the
// slang front end (lhdsuite array_problem.md). Known-failing TWICE:
// prp-equiv-arr_comb_tmp and prp-v2v-arr_comb_tmp are both tagged `fixme`.
//
// This .prp is the VERBATIM `lhd compile arr_comb_tmp.v --emit-dir pyrope:`
// output (headers added). The golden has `always_comb begin t = d;
// arr[0] = t; ... end`; the emitted Pyrope below shows the loss directly —
// `t = 0ub?` where `t = d` should be — so the drop happens on the
// slang->LNAST side (BEFORE tolg): the direct .v->lg->.v round trip refutes
// too (prp-v2v-arr_comb_tmp), unlike arr_comb_mux_const whose direct path is
// fine. SOUNDNESS TRAP: the dropped assignment leaves a don't-care, so the
// native cvc5 `lhd lec` of the two lgraphs returns a VACUOUS PROVEN — only
// the yosys-referenced lgcheck flows (equiv, v2v) see this bug at all.
// The clocked twin (blocking temp inside always_ff feeding a mem store)
// lowers correctly.
pub comb arr_comb_tmp::[timecheck=false](sel:u1, d:u1) -> (o:u1) {
  mut t = 0
  mut arr:[2]u1 = 0
  o = 0ub?
  t = 0ub?
  arr[0] = t
  arr[1] = (~d) & 1
  o = arr[sel]
}
